## Current Synthesis

### Idea

Restore `100k` as the project owner's strategic cockpit. Preserve its deterministic operational
projection, but add the missing owner-authored executive intent and make the normal `ts: 100k`
experience support orientation, strategic review, and selection of the next cycle.

The completed IDEA-0028 implementation optimized complete accounting and avoidance of duplicate
authority until the result became primarily an audit report. This correction preserves that useful
substrate while delivering the executive operating experience IDEA-0028 originally described.

### Why It Matters

The current view can prove that 294 artifacts are accounted for, yet an owner returning to the
project cannot learn its North Star, current strategic horizon, priority landscape, deliberate
non-goals, decisions needed, or why a next cycle is recommended. In an all-terminal project it
shows an apparently healthy field of zeroes followed by a very long ledger. That presentation is
trustworthy but strategically misleading and caused direct operator confusion.

### Desired Outcome

Opening `work/100k.md` or invoking `ts: 100k` lets an owner quickly understand why the project
exists, what "done for now" means, what materially changed, what remains important, which choices
need attention, and which next cycles are credible. The view joins a canonical revisioned
executive-intent source with the existing operational projection.

The main executive view remains concise. Complete accounting remains available through an explicit
ledger drill-down, but the exhaustive ledger is removed from the main `work/100k.md`. An explicit
operator choice routes into existing Ideas, maps, PRMs, campaigns, decisions, outcomes, or planning
order, and resulting evidence and residual gaps return to later executive reviews.

## Constraints And Non-Goals

- Preserve SQLite and file-authority portability and the existing deterministic refresh/check
  safety contract.
- Reuse managed documents, revisions, relationships, outcomes, decisions, planning order, focus
  areas, and the shared project projection rather than introducing another database or lifecycle
  engine.
- Give executive intent a narrow, non-overlapping authority boundary: North Star, current horizon,
  strategic framing, priorities, deliberate non-goals, and review triggers. Existing artifacts
  continue to own execution and lifecycle truth.
- Keep bare `ts: 100k` read-only. Subsequent explicit owner choices may invoke existing guarded
  mutation routes; reading the view alone never selects or starts work.
- Preserve IDEA-0028 and its release as history. Record this work as a residual product correction,
  not a rewritten historical verdict.
- Do not retain the exhaustive Complete Strategic Ledger table in the main executive document.
- Do not make `work/100k.md` manually editable or create a free-standing 100k backlog.

## Possibilities And Tradeoffs

| Possibility | Benefits | Costs / Risks | Evidence / Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Canonical executive-intent record plus generated view | Restores owner authorship without weakening deterministic operational truth | Requires a small new managed document role and clear field ownership | Selected |
| Infer all strategy from existing maps | Avoids a new document role | Completed initiative maps do not provide one living project-level North Star or horizon | Rejected as insufficient |
| Make `work/100k.md` editable | Simple authoring experience | Reintroduces drift and mixed authority | Rejected |
| Keep the full ledger in the main view | One-file completeness | Buries executive meaning beneath hundreds of terminal rows | Rejected; retain as drill-down |

## Open Questions

- Exact command spelling and physical format for the ledger drill-down are implementation details;
  prefer reuse of the existing JSON projection or one deterministic bounded output over a new
  subsystem.
- Determine the smallest schema-compatible representation for the singleton executive-intent
  document during planning; do not add a table if the managed document store can express it.

## Decisions

- The main 100k view is a living strategic cockpit, not a comprehensive artifact dump.
- Add one canonical revisioned Project Executive Intent source with narrow authority.
- Keep `work/100k.md` deterministic and read-only.
- Remove the Complete Strategic Ledger section from the main view while retaining explicit
  drill-down access and complete machine-checkable accounting.
- Make the empty/all-terminal state request a new executive horizon rather than imply there is
  nothing strategically important to decide.
- Treat the month-away orientation scenario as the primary experience acceptance test.
- Preserve IDEA-0028 as history and link this correction back to its unmet original intent.

